course: dictionary
lesson: 4070
title: Geologist
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A geologist is a scientist who studies rocks, soil, minerals and how the Earth was formed and changes. You can spot the word in context: «Geologists tell minerals apart like detectives.» The sentence says a geologist is a kind of detective, so the job is about careful searching and clues.
explain: Geologists look at minerals closely. «Geologists identify minerals by hardness, colour, lustre (shine), streak and how they break.» Each of these is a clue. Hardness is how hard the mineral is, and streak is the colour of its powder.
explain: Geologists also think about very long time. «The Earth is about 4.54 billion years old, a span so huge that geologists call it deep time.» Their work is about the past as well as the present, from volcanoes and earthquakes to fossils.
fact: A geologist is a scientist who studies rocks, soil, minerals and how the Earth was formed and changes.
fact: Geology is the subject a geologist studies.
fact: Geologists look at hardness, colour, lustre (shine), streak and how a mineral breaks.
fact: Streak is the colour of a mineral's powder.
fact: Geologists call the vast span of Earth's history deep time; humans appeared only about 300,000 years ago.
exercise: «Geologists tell minerals apart like detectives.» What do geologists look at to tell minerals apart? | Their smell | *Hardness, colour, shine and how they break | Whether they float on water | Their age in years
exercise: «Geologists test rocks with a drop of acid: limestone fizzes.» What do geologists use to test limestone? | A camera | A magnet | A telescope | *A drop of acid
exercise: Geology is the subject geologists study. Which word means the subject? | deep time | lustre | *geology | streak
test: «Geologists call the vast span of Earth's history deep time.» What is deep time? | *The vast span of Earth's history, far longer than human history | The time between two earthquakes | The time it takes to cook a dinner | A very short holiday
test: What is a mineral's streak? | Its smell | Its weight | *The colour of its powder | How tall it is
exam: A geologist studies rocks, soil and minerals. Who is a geologist? | A teacher who teaches maths | *A scientist who studies rocks and how the Earth changes | A doctor who treats broken bones | A chef who cooks dinners
